Tarrant County needs an integrated justice capability to improve the administration of indigent defense services and information sharing across the criminal justice community. The system should help the Office of Attorney Appointments receive and process requests for appointed counsel, obtain relevant defendant and case information, coordinate attorney appointments, and notify the people and justice organizations involved in each request.

Current Slots:
[
  {
    "name": "project_goals",
    "category": "goals",
    "value": "Make appointed-counsel processing faster, more consistent, and less manual for the Office of Attorney Appointments; improve coordination across the criminal justice community through timely notifications and better sharing of defendant and case details; reduce turnaround time, data entry errors, missing information, and follow-up calls/emails; improve visibility into request status."
  },
  {
    "name": "stakeholder_roles",
    "category": "stakeholders",
    "value": "Office of Attorney Appointments staff; judges or court staff who submit or initiate requests; attorneys who receive appointment information and notifications; jail, clerk, prosecutor, and possibly public defender or other court-connected staff who provide or consume case information. Office staff should review cases, verify eligibility, assign or route appointments, and send notifications; court users should create/submit requests and view relevant status updates; attorneys should receive appointment details and updates but not edit case records; other agencies should have limited access to share or view only the information they are responsible for."
  },
  {
    "name": "functional_needs",
    "category": "functionality",
    "value": "Receive and process requests for appointed counsel; obtain relevant defendant and case information; coordinate attorney appointments; notify involved people and justice organizations; provide request status visibility to users."
  },
  {
